[00:00.00]The diagram above clearly reflects that China has made tremendous achievements in poverty alleviation from 2012 to 2020.
[00:10.15]During this period,
[00:11.83]China’s impoverished rural population decreased considerably from nearly 100 million to nearly zero,
[00:20.50]a decline of 100 million.
[00:22.58]At the same time,
[00:23.96]the poverty headcount ratio also fell from approximately 10% to almost 0%.
[00:30.17]Several primary factors that account for the above-mentioned changes could be summarized as follows.
[00:38.75]To begin with,
[00:39.93]the authorities concerned in China have adopted a combination of conventional and innovative approaches,
[00:48.90]which have helped improve rural education and healthcare.
[00:53.83]What is more,
[00:54.92]our country has put great emphasis on infrastructure establishment in poverty- stricken rural areas,
[01:03.49]which has effectively bridged the gap between the rich and the poor.
[01:09.11]Last but not least,
[01:10.69]the achievements are attributed to China’s speedy economic development during the past several decades.
[01:19.57]In short,
[01:20.36]China’s poverty alleviation campaign is particularly vital,
[01:25.58]both nationally and internationally.
[01:28.84]First of all,
[01:29.92]anti-poverty achievements allow more people to enjoy the advantages of its economic boom.
[01:37.51]In addition,
[01:38.60]the Chinese government has fulfilled its promise of lifting all people out of poverty.
